# lift-patchbox view

I would you like to generate a plan for a new plugin (in the grammars directory). You will look at the corresponding skill for writting plugins.

The plugin will be called "liftpatchbox".

The plugins will recognize and parse LiftPatchShort syntax, i.e. a mutation command language for editing a dictionary.

The liftPatchShort syntax is defined in the lift-patchbox module, in the directory ../lift-patchbox. Please report if you cannot access this directory.

The plugin's pom will declare a dependency towards this module.

The lift-patchbox module already contains a parser for LiftPatchShort syntax. You will check that you will be able to wire this parser to the application.

You will create a new CorpusObject subclass "LexiconEditCommand" in the capacity package and a LexiconCommandImpl in the simple package for holding a LiftPatchShort command. Note that two sub-types of commands exist: normal command (one liner) and "block" command (on several lines)

As for the view:

- in the objectKindTabPane tab, the summary table will give for each command the line it start on and the text of the command.

- in the objectDetailPane, a new view will be created for LexiconEdit command. It will represent the command in LiftPathRef language, which is more verbose and complete.

